+1. A contest can gain more than two competing revisions if multiple workers submit against the same stale base before resolution. Does resolution still choose exactly one revision from the whole set, or can a coordinator reject all of them and request a fresh submission?
+2. A new submission can arrive with a base revision that names a *superseded* (losing) competing revision rather than the visit's actual current revision. Does it join the existing contest, or open a second, independent one against the same visit?
+3. Is resolution strictly "pick one revision as-is," or can a coordinator resolve by lightly editing the chosen revision (e.g. fixing a typo) rather than submitting yet another worker revision first?
+4. While a visit is contested, is its last-agreed current revision eligible for the Friday export, or does any open contest hold the whole visit out regardless of which fields the competing revisions touch?
